{"name":"Mille-Feuille","hex":"#efc87d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mille-feuille","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of pastry made of several layers of puff pastry usually filled with cream or custard, and topped with icing or sugar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mille-feuille"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mille-feuille","blocks":[{"text":"A mille-feuille, also known as Napoleon in Russia and other post-Soviet states, as well as in North America, vanilla slice and custard slice in the United Kingdom, as well as Australia and New Zealand, is a French dessert made of puff pastry layered with pastry cream. Its modern form was influenced by improvements made by Marie-Antoine Carême."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Mille-feuille_fran%C3%A7ais_1.jpg/330px-Mille-feuille_fran%C3%A7ais_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mille-feuille","wikidata":"Q12491"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Strawberry_Napoleon.jpg/500px-Strawberry_Napoleon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Strawberry_Napoleon.jpg/1280px-Strawberry_Napoleon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Strawberry_Napoleon.jpg/500px-Strawberry_Napoleon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Homemade mille-feuille with fresh strawberries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStrawberry_Napoleon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Slide-mille-feuille.jpg/500px-Slide-mille-feuille.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Sli